# UI / presentation — game interface, not SaaS

This is a **Pokémon-game-inspired** companion UI: modern retro/device panels, light pastels (white / pale blue / pink), navy text, cyan/pink accents, restrained gold for rewards, rounded panels, deliberate borders, subtle depth, meaningful fanfare.

Avoid: corporate dashboards, giant empty whitespace, huge left navs, analytics card walls, dark Twitch-dashboard restyles, rainbow selected states, glassmorphism everywhere, excessive gradients/ornament.

## Layout

- Grid for true 2D matrices; Flex for toolbars, button groups, nav, linear rows
- Do not mechanically swap Grid↔Flex
- Prefer stable parent geometry, `minmax(0, 1fr)`, reserved media size, controlled overflow
- **No layout shift** when switching tabs / Buy·Sell / filters / selected cosmetics / async data
- Dynamic strings: `min-width: 0`, wrap or truncate appropriately — do not truncate blindly

Async UX: establish stable containers → load/decode → present. Do not animate position just because data arrived.

## Responsive QA (typical)

1920×1080 · 2560×1440 · half-screen / constrained desktop · ~390px mobile  
No horizontal overflow; touch-usable controls; do not shrink text into unreadability.

## Sprites

Use established presentation helpers (`pc-presentation`, pokedex presentation, alpha/safe envelope). Do not invent one-off crop CSS unless the system cannot represent the case. Do not force identical apparent heights.

## Motion / a11y

Respect `play-perf` modes (AUTO/HIGH/BALANCED/LOW) and `prefers-reduced-motion`.  
Dialogs: keyboard, focus-visible, semantics, focus trap, Escape when safe, restore focus. Do not encode state by color alone.
